Patch T6 oracles (rung 1b, task T6): protect eng-session's hash-equality
test, and run criterion 11's three test files as the `wire-session` step.

- crates/eng-session/tests/hash_equality.rs joins protected.toml and
  .github/CODEOWNERS (proposal 8, amendments 11 and 19): criterion 11's
  "the session gives the same hashes as stepping the simulation
  directly". Its header now says it is protected.
- X7's `wire-session` step (amendment 18): `cargo xtask ci --job test`
  runs eng-net-wire's `golden` and `never_panic` and eng-session's
  `hash_equality` in one `cargo test`, after `live-input`. A row of
  `HARNESSES` now lists its test files. The unit test checks that each
  file exists, and that no other package in the same step has a test
  target of that name (`tests/<name>.rs`, `tests/<name>/main.rs` or a
  `[[test]]` entry), which the one `cargo test` would also run.
- docs/ARCHITECTURE.md names the new step.

Base: main with the commit that adds this file (rung 1b, T6). At the repo
root, run `git apply` with this file, then `cargo xtask quick` and `cargo
xtask ci --job test`. PROGRESS.md, session 17's T6 entry, says how it was
tested.
Text before the first `diff --git` line is ignored by `git apply`.

